My tablet app has the following tasks:
 
- Provide an interface to the user, with a pinch and drag display with clickable nodes, 
other stateful buttons and a couple of alternative pages like a settings page.
 
- Extract coordinate information from .dxf drawing files.
 
- Send and receive data through the USB-C port to/from an ESP32 NOW WiFi dongle. Data rates peaking at 10KB/s.
 
- Be downloadeable as an android app.
 
- The tablet is a OnePlus Pad Go running OxygenOS.
 
The tech stack will be Kotlin + Jetpack Compose, native Android. 
The DXF will be processed using Chaquopy + the ezdxf Python library. 
Chaquopy embeds a CPython runtime into the APK and allows the calling of Python from Kotlin.